-- P2-art-4a: Article 4a of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, and the paragraph of Article 10 it took over from.
-- THE HAND-OVER. The Omnibus inserted Article 4a (Chapter I, in the text from 27 July 2026) and deleted Article 10(5). Article 10(5) as enacted let the providers of high-risk AI systems exceptionally process special
-- categories of personal data to ensure bias detection and correction, on six conditions; Article 4a(1) says the same in nearly the same words, and Article 4a(2) extends the permission to the providers and deployers of
-- other AI systems and models and to the deployers of high-risk AI systems. `Art 4a(1) the provider may exceptionally process special categories of personal data` dispatches on the version in force:
-- as enacted it reads Article 10(5) (Chapter III Section 2, which never applied while that text was the text: fork F-10-5-dead), as amended it reads Article 4a(1) (Chapter I, from 2 February 2025).
-- Each text is also in its own function with no date, so that the old text is tested through its own function.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE the processing is permitted on these facts; JUST FALSE a condition the text makes necessary is not met; NOTHING not covered (not a high-risk AI system's provider, not special categories of personal data, not strictly necessary, not yet applicable, or the paragraph is not in the text on that date).
-- Borrowed terms are plain inputs: the GDPR provisions, special categories of personal data (the keel's Art 3(37) computes it in the seat), strict necessity.

§ `Article 10(5) as enacted: the permission before the Omnibus`

-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:765 | 5. To the extent that it is strictly necessary for the purpose of ensuring bias detection and correction in relation to the high-risk AI systems in accordance with paragraph (2), points (f) and (g) of this Article, the providers of such systems may exceptionally process special categories of personal data, subject to appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons. In addition to the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, all the following conditions must be met in order for such processing to occur:
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:767 | the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:769 | the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of the personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:771 | the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured, protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:773 | the special categories of personal data are not to be transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:775 | the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:777 | the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data.
@ref Art 10(5) as enacted (deleted by the Omnibus) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:765-777)
-- VERSION as enacted. Deleted from 27 July 2026 (consolidated lines 305-306: "▼M1 DELETED"); Article 4a(1) takes over. No date and no gate: the dispatcher below applies Article 113.
-- "in accordance with paragraph (2), points (f) and (g) of this Article" is the same reference as Article 4a(1)'s "Article 10(2), points (f) and (g)": one input.
GIVEN `the AI system is a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a provider of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data processed are special categories of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in relation to high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 10(2), points (f) and (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10(5) as enacted the provider may exceptionally process special categories of personal data` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the AI system is a high-risk AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to high-risk AI systems" and "providers of such systems": the permission is for the providers of high-risk AI systems
    ELSE IF NOT (`the party is a provider of the AI system`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "providers of such systems may exceptionally process": the permission is the provider's
         ELSE IF NOT (`the data processed are special categories of personal data`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may exceptionally process special categories of personal data"
              ELSE IF NOT (`the processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in relation to high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 10(2), points (f) and (g)`)
                   THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the extent strictly necessary": a grant limited by its own wording; split site (ii), fork F-4a-1-necessary
                   ELSE JUST (`appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` AND `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` AND `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` AND `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` AND `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` AND `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` AND `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` AND `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all the following conditions must be met in order for such processing to occur"


§ `Article 4a(1): providers of high-risk AI systems`

-- src:159 | 1. To the extent strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in relation to high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 10(2), points (f) and (g), of this Regulation, providers of such systems may exceptionally process special categories of personal data, subject to appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons. In addition to the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, all the following conditions shall be met in order for such processing to occur:
-- src:160 | (a) the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data;
-- src:161 | (b) the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation;
-- src:162 | (c) the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations;
-- src:163 | (d) the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties;
-- src:164 | (e) the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first; and
-- src:165 | (f) the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data.
@ref Art 4a(1) (src:159-165)
-- VERSION as amended. A grant ("may exceptionally process"): the processing the text permits. The six conditions and the safeguards are necessary ("all the following conditions shall be met in order for such processing to occur"),
-- so an unmet one is the text's own no (JUST FALSE); strict necessity and the other limits of who and what are limits of the grant (NOTHING when they fail): split site (ii), forks F-4a-1-conditions and F-4a-1-necessary.
-- "In addition to the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable" is read as a further condition: compliance with those provisions is a plain input (fork F-4a-1-gdpr).
