§ `Article 4a(2): other AI systems and models, and deployers of high-risk AI systems`

-- src:166 | 2. Providers and deployers of other AI systems and models and deployers of high-risk AI systems may exceptionally process special categories of personal data to the extent that:
-- src:167 | (a) such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations; and
-- src:168 | (b) all of the conditions and safeguards set out in paragraph 1 are applied.
@ref Art 4a(2) (src:166-168)
-- Inserted by the Omnibus: no as-enacted text, so NOTHING before 27 July 2026 (silent). "may exceptionally process ... to the extent that": a grant; the paragraph reaches three kinds of party (the first and second limbs read "providers and deployers of other AI systems and models" as
-- each of the two roles for both systems and models: fork F-4a-2-parties). (b) "all of the conditions and safeguards set out in paragraph 1 are applied" is computed from paragraph 1's own facts: the safeguards, the GDPR provisions and the six conditions.
