`Art 4a(2) the provider or deployer may exceptionally process special categories of personal data` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter I "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the Omnibus inserted this provision; the text as enacted has none
         WHEN `as amended` THEN         -- VERSION as amended
             IF NOT (`the data processed are special categories of personal data`)
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may exceptionally process special categories of personal data"
             ELSE IF NOT (`such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations`)
                  THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent that (a) such processing is strictly necessary": a grant limited by its own wording; split site (ii), fork F-4a-2-extent
                  ELSE IF NOT (`the party is a provider of an AI system or of an AI model other than a high-risk AI system` OR `the party is a deployer of an AI system or of an AI model other than a high-risk AI system` OR `the party is a deployer of a high-risk AI system`)
                       THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers and deployers of other AI systems and models and deployers of high-risk AI systems": a list the paragraph names; a provider of a high-risk AI system is under paragraph 1
                       ELSE JUST (`appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` AND `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` AND `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` AND `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` AND `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` AND `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` AND `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` AND `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may exceptionally process special categories of personal data to the extent that: ... (b) all of the conditions and safeguards set out in paragraph 1 are applied"

-- src:169 | This paragraph does not create any obligation to conduct such bias detection and correction.
@ref Art 4a(2) last sentence (src:169)
-- A flat negative ("does not create any obligation"): JUST FALSE once the paragraph is in the text and Chapter I applies.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4a(2) last sentence the paragraph creates an obligation to conduct bias detection and correction` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 2 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter I "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the Omnibus inserted this provision; the text as enacted has none
         WHEN `as amended` THEN         -- VERSION as amended
             JUST (FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph does not create any obligation to conduct such bias detection and correction"
